1
00:03:24,444 --> 00:03:30,444
His struggle for fame was over. His fight for respect was just beginning.

2
00:06:48,888 --> 00:06:54,888
Tender Mercies is a drama, music, romance film directed by Bruce Beresford.

3
00:10:13,333 --> 00:10:19,333
Alchoholic former country singer Mac Sledge makes
friends with a young widow and her son.

4
00:13:37,777 --> 00:13:43,777
The friendship enables him to find inspiration to resume his career.

5
00:17:02,222 --> 00:17:08,222
Mac Sledge, played by Robert Duvall.

6
00:20:26,666 --> 00:20:32,666
Rosa Lee, played by Tess Harper.

7
00:23:51,111 --> 00:23:57,111
Dixie, played by Betty Buckley.

8
00:27:15,555 --> 00:27:21,555
Harry, played by Wilford Brimley.

9
00:30:40,000 --> 00:30:46,000
Sue Anne, played by Ellen Barkin.

10
00:34:04,444 --> 00:34:10,444
Sonny, played by Allan Hubbard.

11
00:37:28,888 --> 00:37:34,888
Tender Mercies is a 1983 American drama film directed by
Bruce Beresford and written by Horton Foote.

12
00:40:53,333 --> 00:40:59,333
It stars Robert Duvall as singer-songwriter Mac Sledge, a former country music star whose
career and relationship with his ex-wife and daughter were wrecked by alcoholism.

13
00:44:17,777 --> 00:44:23,777
Recovering from his affliction, Sledge seeks to turn his life around through
his relationship with a young widow and her son in rural Texas.

14
00:47:42,222 --> 00:47:48,222
The supporting cast includes Tess Harper, Betty Buckley,
Wilford Brimley, Ellen Barkin and Allan Hubbard.

15
00:51:06,666 --> 00:51:12,666
Financed by EMI Films, Tender Mercies was shot largely in Waxahachie, Texas.

16
00:54:31,111 --> 00:54:37,111
The script was rejected by several American directors
before the Australian Beresford accepted it.

17
00:57:55,555 --> 00:58:01,555
Duvall, who sang his own songs in the film, drove more than 600 miles (1,000 km) throughout the state,
tape recording local accents and playing in country music bands to prepare for the role.

18
01:01:20,000 --> 01:01:26,000
He and Beresford repeatedly clashed during production, at one point prompting the
director to walk off the set and reportedly consider quitting the film.

19
01:04:44,444 --> 01:04:50,444
The film encompasses several themes, including the importance of love and family, the possibility of spiritual
resurrection amid death and the concept of redemption through Mac Sledge's conversion to Christianity.

20
01:08:08,888 --> 01:08:14,888
Following poor test screening results, distributor Universal Pictures made little effort to publicise
Tender Mercies, which Duvall attributed to the studio's lack of understanding of country music.

21
01:11:33,333 --> 01:11:39,333
The film was released on March 4, 1983, in a limited number of theatres.

22
01:14:57,777 --> 01:15:03,777
Although unsuccessful at the box office, it was critically acclaimed and
earned five Academy Award nominations, including for Best Picture.

23
01:18:22,222 --> 01:18:28,222
At the 56th Academy Awards.

24
01:21:46,666 --> 01:21:52,666
Tender Mercies won Oscars for Best Original Screenplay for Foote
and Duvall won the Academy Award for Best Actor.

25
01:25:11,111 --> 01:25:17,111
The film explores themes of country music, guitar,
texas, alcoholism, southern baptist.

26
01:28:35,555 --> 01:28:41,555
The tone is emotional.
